OpenLight attribution and modification notice
-------------------------------------------
Reference revision: 11de0593cc8091933ad76d1d6d873f7dee537f15
Source: https://github.com/luxgrain/GALOSH

OpenLight used standalone/galosh_cpu.h and the corresponding Vulkan/OpenCL
noise-statistics and transform sources as references for:
- same-CFA second-difference MAD noise estimation and a lower-envelope noise fit;
- a continuous signed-shadow extension of the generalized Anscombe transform;
- the eight-sample Kaiser window used for overlap aggregation.

The related OpenLight files are src/lib/denoise/bayer/noise.ts,
bayer/statistics.wgsl, bayer/variance.wgsl, and the WINDOW constants in
src/lib/denoise/collaborative.wgsl. These are substantially modified TypeScript/WGSL adaptations:
per-phase sampled fitting replaces the upstream estimator, the forward transform
is offset and numerically rearranged, the inverse is asymptotic rather than the
upstream lookup table, and GPU statistics use cooperative bitonic sorting.
The GALOSH denoising library and its complete processing pipeline are not bundled.

Retain this notice and the accompanying Apache-2.0 license for these adaptations.
